  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Asia Sustainable and Alternative Energy Program (ASTAEMDTF)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">&quot;The ASTAE MDTF will contribute to encouraging and increasing WB client  countries# (i) adoption of solutions for scaling up deployment of  renewable energy technologies, (ii) adoption of solutions for scaling  up use of energy efficiency technologies, (iii) increased access to  modern energy services, and (iv) enhanced policy decisions and  institutional capacity to plan, manage, and regulate the energy  sector.
 The ASTAE program will be assessed by the following indicators that  measure the leverage of the MDTF grants on WB investments:
 #	catalytic effect of ASTAE grants on WB project, measured by total  lending that benefited from the ASTAE support;
 #	amount of new installed capacity, increase in generation of  electricity from renewable energy sources, and the share of these  sources in the energy mix, under the WB projects supported by ASTAE;
 #	amount of energy savings resulting from energy efficiency  improvements under the WB projects supported by ASTAE;
 #	increase in number of households with access to modern or improved  energy services under the WB projects supported by ASTAE;
 #	amount of greenhouse gas emissions avoided under the WB projects  supported by ASTAE;
 #	number of countries in which policies and investment strategies were  influenced by ASTAE.
 All indicators are based on measurable WB projects metrics. Specific  targets for each indicator are set in the ASTAE business plan, in  accordance to the strategy adopted in coordination with the donors.&quot;</narrative>
  </description>
